# ============================================================================
# vpn.env.example  —  TEMPLATE (safe to commit). Copy to `vpn.env` and fill in.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   cp vpn.env.example vpn.env      # then paste your key below
#
# `vpn.env` is gitignored; this example is NOT. Never put a real key here.
#
# The SearXNG stack routes its traffic through a Proton VPN US node (gluetun)
# so Google stops returning 403 on image search. This file supplies the one
# secret gluetun needs: your Proton WireGuard private key.
#
# HOW TO GET THE KEY (paid Proton plan required):
#   1. Log in at https://account.protonvpn.com  (the dashboard, not the app).
#   2. Downloads → WireGuard configuration.
#   3. Name it (e.g. "searxng-us"), Platform = GNU/Linux, pick any US server.
#   4. Create → open the downloaded .conf → copy the [Interface] PrivateKey.
#   5. Paste it below as WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY.
#
# Server selection is automatic (SERVER_COUNTRIES=United States in
# docker-compose.yml), so any US server's config works. See VPN-EGRESS.md and
# the README "Optional: Route SearXNG through Proton VPN" section for details.
# ============================================================================

WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=
